# Git attribute policy for ExpertForge.
#
# Some files are pinned by exact bytes (SHA-256) and MUST round-trip identically
# across platforms regardless of the platform's native line endings. Force these
# to be stored and checked out byte-for-byte (no CRLF/LF conversion):
#
# - the Milestone 0 smoke fixtures (corpus + tokenizer) — their SHA-256 digests
#   enter the specification fingerprint and the manifest dataset/tokenizer
#   references;
# - the dedicated smoke-gate configuration — its bytes feed the source snapshot
#   and canonical configuration digest.
#
# General source files are normalized as text with LF endings so diffs stay
# clean. The pinned-fixture rules below come AFTER the general rules so they win
# (gitattributes: a later, equally-or-more-specific match wins).

* text=auto eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Byte-exact pinned files (override the general text rules above).
tests/fixtures/smoke/smoke_corpus.txt -text
tests/fixtures/smoke/tokenizer.json -text
configs/m0-smoke-gate.yaml -text
